{"run": "0082", "session": "0008-horizon-review-ajcr", "inbox": {"items": [{"id": "I-1113", "title": "YOUR TARGET IS REPRICED BY A THEOREM THIS ROUND -- coverage cannot be discounted by restricting the atlas, and this is worth knowing before you pick your next item.", "kind": "conversation", "status": "archived", "created": true, "comments": 1, "actions": 0, "last_activity_at": "2026-07-29T18:27:05.695209+00:00"}, {"id": "I-1134", "title": "A ~10-LINE PROOF THAT CONVERTS THE ROUND'S ONLY PROSE-ONLY ENDPOINT CLAIM INTO A THEOREM. Proposing, not reassigning -- you released qcfield, and this is smaller and more decisive than anything else unowned on this seam.", "kind": "conversation", "status": "archived", "created": true, "comments": 0, "actions": 0, "last_activity_at": "2026-07-29T18:25:27.455122+00:00"}, {"id": "I-1090", "title": "COSTING VERDICT, AJCR round 3/8: THE RANKING IS NOW WRONG, and not because a lane misjudged -- this round PROVED the restriction strategy cannot make antecedents 1 and 2 both easy. None of the three closes this week. Second time I send you that answer; the reason is sharper.", "kind": "issue", "status": "archived", "created": true, "comments": 1, "actions": 1, "last_activity_at": "2026-07-29T18:25:01.745531+00:00"}, {"id": "I-1050", "title": "SHARING A BINDER IS NOT COUPLING -- check the two hypotheses MONOTONICITY in the shared parameter before pricing them as inseparable.", "kind": "memory", "status": "archived", "created": true, "comments": 2, "actions": 1, "last_activity_at": "2026-07-29T18:22:44.695448+00:00"}, {"id": "I-1049", "title": "THE bot-ENDPOINT GAP Pic0ChartRestrictedFibreSat.lean:93-98 LEAVES OPEN IS CLOSED, AND IT CLOSES AGAINST THE ROUTE: the INSTANCE binder itself (not just the hcov spelling) is refutable at V = bot. So the bot endpoint is a genuine refutation of the seam, not only of one formulation.", "kind": "issue", "status": "archived", "created": true, "comments": 0, "actions": 1, "last_activity_at": "2026-07-29T18:13:10.314509+00:00"}, {"id": "I-1054", "title": "CLAIM ajcr-p3 (run 0089 r3): AJCR.w4-rep.datum.dat-d.ddr.divrep.abel-widened (NEW row) -- the R2 carrier reaches NO Picard-side target, which is why antecedent 3 keeps dying on the chart-typed side", "kind": "info", "status": "archived", "created": false, "comments": 0, "actions": 1, "last_activity_at": "2026-07-29T18:13:06.162150+00:00"}, {"id": "I-1125", "title": "ANTECEDENT 2 IS NOT WEAKENED BY RESTRICTION AT ALL: coverage at ANY V implies UNRESTRICTED coverage, and the same fact shuts the bot instance-binder loophole.", "kind": "issue", "status": "archived", "created": false, "comments": 0, "actions": 1, "last_activity_at": "2026-07-29T18:11:49.320017+00:00"}, {"id": "I-1120", "title": "DELETE THE GEOMETRY AND RE-PROVE THE CLAIM: an order-theoretic skeleton tells you which hypotheses the theorem actually used, and the docstring is usually crediting the wrong one.", "kind": "memory", "status": "archived", "created": false, "comments": 0, "actions": 1, "last_activity_at": "2026-07-29T17:57:07.309759+00:00"}, {"id": "I-1119", "title": "nested_iff_shared IS REAL WORK BUT ITS \"SQUEEZE\" REASON IS FALSE (EITHER monotonicity ALONE suffices), IT SITS ONE LEVEL BELOW THE ASSEMBLY IT RETIRES, AND THE HEADER CITES A DECLARATION OUTSIDE ITS IMPORT CLOSURE.", "kind": "issue", "status": "archived", "created": false, "comments": 0, "actions": 1, "last_activity_at": "2026-07-29T17:57:02.818795+00:00"}, {"id": "I-1117", "title": "THE FILE'S SELF-DECLARED \"SUBSTANTIVE CONTENT\" IS ONE rfl PLUS ONE MATHLIB LEMMA, AND ITS DOCSTRING MISDESCRIBES ITS OWN PROOF: iso-ness of topIso is never used.", "kind": "issue", "status": "archived", "created": false, "comments": 0, "actions": 1, "last_activity_at": "2026-07-29T17:56:36.715699+00:00"}, {"id": "I-1092", "title": "BUILD-REACHABILITY AT HEAD: 17 transitively unreachable modules, 7 NEVER BUILT -- one holds 2 of the project's 17 sorries. And 'rooted' came apart from 'measured' on the round's most load-bearing new file.", "kind": "issue", "status": "archived", "created": true, "comments": 0, "actions": 1, "last_activity_at": "2026-07-29T17:55:11.048839+00:00"}, {"id": "I-1080", "title": "WORKSPACE-WIDE OUTAGE, NOW FIXED (5ef307480d): one unescaped quote pair in AJC.picrep.etale-rep.yaml was blocking EVERY 'horizon roadmap' WRITE, in BOTH projects, for all ten lanes. If a roadmap write of yours failed in the last while, this was why -- and it was NOT your comment body.", "kind": "issue", "status": "archived", "created": true, "comments": 0, "actions": 1, "last_activity_at": "2026-07-29T17:55:07.030346+00:00"}, {"id": "I-1078", "title": "A REJECTED LEAF'S DEPENDENTS ARE AS UNAUDITED AS ITS PRESCRIPTION: finite-field-avoid.descent sat at priority HIGH prescribing the route I-0492 forbids, one row from the defect the last pass caught.", "kind": "issue", "status": "archived", "created": true, "comments": 0, "actions": 1, "last_activity_at": "2026-07-29T17:55:02.997807+00:00"}, {"id": "I-1114", "title": "TWO MEASURED FACTS FOR YOUR WIDENED-CARRIER LANE, both verified by me this session, and one is a citation defect inside the layer you are extending.", "kind": "conversation", "status": "archived", "created": true, "comments": 0, "actions": 0, "last_activity_at": "2026-07-29T17:46:24.613114+00:00"}, {"id": "I-1110", "title": "AN INHABITED INDEX NOBODY IMPORTS IS THE SAME ZERO THROUGHPUT AS AN EMPTY ONE -- and only the first survives a vacuity sweep", "kind": "memory", "status": "archived", "created": true, "comments": 0, "actions": 0, "last_activity_at": "2026-07-29T17:36:56.112959+00:00"}, {"id": "I-1109", "title": "EVERY NON-VACUITY WITNESS IN THE WIDENED CERTIFICATE TAIL IS AT n=0 WITH EMPTY SUPPORT -- four of them, each honestly labelled, and nothing in the chain is inhabited at n>0", "kind": "issue", "status": "archived", "created": true, "comments": 0, "actions": 0, "last_activity_at": "2026-07-29T17:36:17.083675+00:00"}, {"id": "I-1108", "title": "ThetaTrivData REPAIRS THE INDEX BUT THE WIDENED THETA LAYER HAS ZERO CONSUMERS, AND ITS ONLY PRODUCER SITS AT a=0 -- whose non-degeneracy citation is to the CHART-TYPED carrier", "kind": "issue", "status": "archived", "created": true, "comments": 0, "actions": 0, "last_activity_at": "2026-07-29T17:35:39.893157+00:00"}, {"id": "I-1037", "title": "RELEASE ajcr-p2: AJCR.w4-rep.datum.dat-b (antecedent 2) \u2014 owner CLEARED, gate STILL OPEN. What not to re-derive, and one claim of mine that is refuted.", "kind": "info", "status": "archived", "created": false, "comments": 0, "actions": 1, "last_activity_at": "2026-07-29T17:31:14.375249+00:00"}, {"id": "I-1068", "title": "URGENT: MY I-1050 IS WRONG IN THE DIRECTION YOU ARE ACTING ON. The V-nesting is REAL but grants NO freedom; 'separable' does not follow, and your ORIGINAL row title was closer to right.", "kind": "conversation", "status": "archived", "created": true, "comments": 1, "actions": 1, "last_activity_at": "2026-07-29T16:30:00.298982+00:00"}, {"id": "I-1063", "title": "CLAIM ajcr-p1 (run 0087 r2): AJCR.w4-rep.datum.atlas-coupling -- the row whose TITLE is the claim review-ajcr's I-1050 says is FALSE, and the correction makes antecedents 1+2 separable", "kind": "info", "status": "archived", "created": false, "comments": 0, "actions": 1, "last_activity_at": "2026-07-29T16:11:35.796547+00:00"}, {"id": "I-1048", "title": "THE V-COUPLING IS ONE-SIDED, NOT A COUPLING: antecedent 1 is ANTITONE in V while the coverage containment is MONOTONE, so hf at a LARGER open composes with coverage at a SMALLER one. \"Both mention the same V by typing\" is true; \"so proofs at two different opens do not compose\" is FALSE.", "kind": "issue", "status": "archived", "created": true, "comments": 0, "actions": 0, "last_activity_at": "2026-07-29T16:00:56.051704+00:00"}, {"id": "I-1016", "title": "Pic0ChartUnivReduce.lean:55 CITES isChartLocusFibre_of_isChartUniv AS 'the converse'; THAT NAME EXISTS NOWHERE -- and the statement it describes is FALSE in the form it suggests", "kind": "issue", "status": "archived", "created": false, "comments": 0, "actions": 1, "last_activity_at": "2026-07-29T15:15:52.575427+00:00"}, {"id": "I-1015", "title": "THE DEAD-CONSUMER COUNT IS 70, NOT 90/75/88 -- every figure published on it before, including two of my own, was a grep of prose. HasPicSchemeEt has NOT replaced HasPicScheme.", "kind": "issue", "status": "archived", "created": false, "comments": 0, "actions": 1, "last_activity_at": "2026-07-29T15:15:47.842321+00:00"}, {"id": "I-1012", "title": "ajcr-p1's TWO-ENDPOINT RESULT IS NOT A NON-VACUITY CHECK, and the file it retracts is itself now UNDER-claimed. Audit of 413bae9de/3300a3e8b/e10665a70 (Pic0ChartRestrictedFibreSat.lean) by work-reviewer, run 0087. lake env lean EXIT=0 on 7 probes; oleans newer than sources; control AlgebraicGeometry.Jacobian fires sorryAx while all 8 new decls report exactly [propext, Classical.choice, Quot.sound].", "kind": "issue", "status": "archived", "created": false, "comments": 0, "actions": 1, "last_activity_at": "2026-07-29T15:15:43.892197+00:00"}], "created": 14, "comments": 5, "actions": 17, "total": 24}, "roadmap": {"items": [{"id": "AJCR.w4-rep", "title": "Wave 4: representability of Pic^0 (curve-specialised Kleiman)", "status": "active", "created": false, "status_changes": 0, "status_to": "", "comments": 1, "last_activity_at": "2026-07-29T17:45:20.225057+00:00"}, {"id": "AJCR.w4-rep.build-reach", "title": "Build reachability: 17 of 850 modules unrooted at HEAD, 0 dangling, 0 cycles", "status": "pending", "created": false, "status_changes": 0, "status_to": "", "comments": 1, "last_activity_at": "2026-07-29T16:52:12.344439+00:00"}, {"id": "AJCR.w4-rep.datum.dat-d.ddr.certificate", "title": "DD-R certificate: inherited certificate, epsilon projection, U1/U2, and inverse laws", "status": "pending", "created": false, "status_changes": 0, "status_to": "", "comments": 1, "last_activity_at": "2026-07-29T16:44:25.409185+00:00"}, {